Remember that I did not only include the Nasties. I included
everything. Even after including everything there were only a very few
monsters left. So what happens is that the code will roll for a nasty.
If the nasty is a spellcaster you get that. If it is a genocided
monster it will roll again. But this time it will roll from the list
of all the monsters. In this case you get to the list that I created.

So the end result is that the code will save you if you have genocided
some monsters but not if you have genocided many monsters. Previously
a summon storm was possible if you genocided a few nasties, but now
it is only likely if you genocide too many classes, not necessarily
nasties.
Though you may need to be slightly unlucky. But with 5 endgame levels
it
becomes reasonably likely.

